{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>שא נא כליך</b> — that is, sharpen your knife, like משיאה על גבי חברתה (raising one sword upon another)." "<b>וצא</b> — twice in the Masorah: וצא השדה, וצא הלחם. As stated in Bereshit Rabbah: כליך — this is Babylon, for the vessels of the Temple were brought there. תליך — this is Media, on account of Haman who came from Media. קשתך — this is Greece. השדה — this is Edom. And he hinted to him all four kingdoms that are destined to fall into Israel's hand, for HaShem will fight them — and that is what is written: וצא הלחם, against Amalek." "<b>ציד</b> — written צידה with an extra heh, to teach that HaShem taught the laws of slaughter and the five signs of purity in a bird: it does not prey. an extra toe. a crop. a gizzard that peels. it does not split its feet. And in a wild animal: split hoof. chews the cud. and it has no upper teeth. horns. and its flesh goes crosswise beneath the tail."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "תליך read as a variant/phonetic form of תליך (your quiver); the Aramaic/Hebrew form as written is preserved.", 2 "The phrase 'ובשרה הולך שתי וערב תחת העוקץ' is rendered hyper-literally; the anatomical reference is preserved without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:11.065115452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}